#
# Counter-example for math:FlagshipScenarioShape: a math:FlagshipScenario that binds
# ALL FOUR links — math:demonstratedByExample, math:demonstratedByCompetency,
# math:guardedByCounterExample, AND math:enforcesFailureClass — so every one of the four
# sh:minCount branches is satisfied, but math:enforcesFailureClass names math:Set, a real
# class that is NOT a math:MathConformanceFailure subclass. Only the sh:sparql subclass
# check fires, so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent (and no other
# finding, math:UnwiredFlagshipScenario): an acceptance scenario whose enforcing failure
# class is not a typed conformance failure is unwired by value, not by cardinality.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecFlagshipNonFailureClass).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:nonFailureClassScenario a math:FlagshipScenario ;
    math:demonstratedByExample "examples/e8-symmetry.ttl" ;
    math:demonstratedByCompetency <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/tests/cqE8RootSystem> ;
    math:guardedByCounterExample "tests/counter-examples/e8-wrong-weyl-order.ttl" ;
    math:enforcesFailureClass math:Set .
